<Page title="Terms of service">
  <p><strong>Draft.</strong> These are the service terms already in use, written down. Replace with the owner's final wording before launch.</p>
  <h2>Service</h2>
  <p>Recurring visits are weekly or every other week on a set day. We scoop the whole yard each visit and bag the waste; haul-away is $5 per visit, otherwise the bag is left in your trash can.</p>
  <h2>Access</h2>
  <p>Please leave gates unlocked on your service day and let us know about any dog that should be kept inside. If we can't get into the yard, the visit is still billed.</p>
  <h2>Weather</h2>
  <p>If the weather makes the yard unsafe or unworkable on your day, we come within the next day or two. Your bill doesn't change.</p>
  <h2>Billing</h2>
  <p>Invoices go out at the end of the month and can be paid by Zelle, cash, credit or debit card, or check. If a bill is still open at the end of the month, service pauses until it's settled. Yards over 12,000 sq ft carry a $50 monthly surcharge. Restarting after a lapse of three weeks or more carries a $40 start-up fee.</p>
  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Call or text {site.phone}.</p>
</Page>
